  "prefLabel": "En 1012.10 Timelines",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1012.10 Timelines.\n\n(a) For a group of DERs with no more than 3 applicants, an aggregated nameplate capacity of 10 MW or less, and estimated aggregate system modifications less than $1,500,000, the utility shall complete the group study within 100 business days of the applicants’ delivery of the executed group study agreements.\n\n(b) For a group of DERs with no more than 5 applicants, an aggregated nameplate capacity of 25 MW or less, and estimated aggregate system modifications less than $1,500,000, the utility shall complete the group study within 125 business days of the applicants’ delivery of the executed group study agreements.\n\n(c) For all other groups of DERs the utility shall complete the group study within 160 business days of the applicants’ delivery of the executed group study agreements.\n\n(d) The utility shall be provided with an additional 60 business days to complete the group study if substation upgrades are required.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
